Z||000000||Cooter||12-18-2000||11:30 PM||||While checking on all the crap that was never done to the wife's car, I ran the 88 Fiero through the NHTSA database and found this TSB:<BR>Service Bulletin Number: 91312 <BR>Bulletin Sequence Number: 002<BR>Date of Bulletin: 9102<BR>NHTSA Item Number: SB022157 <BR>Make: PONTIAC<BR>Model: FIERO<BR>Year: 1988<BR>Component: STEERING:POWER ASSIST<BR>Summary: REDUCED POWER STEERING ASSIST AT LOW AMBIENT TEMPERATURES-NEW POWER STEERING FLU ID-ALL PONTIAC MODELS CE<P>I hate it when my Fiero's power steering gives out at low temperatures! I bet the dealer would have a stroke if you took your car in and asked to have the car checked for compliance to that TSB!||||reg||1
